# quant-backtest

Apply the quant-backtest skill when the request matches its scope.

Capabilities:
- apply quant backtest methods within explicit quant boundaries
- audit data, code, configuration, validation, costs, execution assumptions, and failure modes
- produce and validate a quant artifact with evidence, provenance, hashes, and a bounded verdict

Stop when: Required manifests and hashes are recorded, point-in-time and leakage controls pass, validation and cost assumptions are evidenced, deterministic replay and known-failure fixtures are evaluated, and the verdict is PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED, or NOT-RUN.
